.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt SBOM-GENERATOR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sbom-generator
.Nd generate SPDX documents from installed package SBOM files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c
.Op Ar package ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads the SBOM files that each package installs.
It creates two SPDX documents for each SBOM file.
.Pp
Each SBOM file is a
.Xr pc 5
file in the
.Pa share/sbom/pc
directory.
The name of the file is the name of the package or subpackage, followed by
.Dq .pc .
.Pp
.Nm
reads the
.Dq Requires
field of each file.
It adds all dependencies to the document.
It adds the dependencies of each dependency, and so on.
.Pp
If you give no
.Ar package ,
.Nm
processes all SBOM files in the
.Pa share/sbom/pc
directory.
If you give one or more
.Ar package
names, it processes only those packages.
.Pp
.Nm
creates these files for each package:
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa spdx-3.0.1/package.jsonld"
.It Pa spdx-2.2/package.spdx
An SPDX 2.2 document in tag-value format.
.Nm
uses
.Xr bomtool 1
to create it.
.It Pa spdx-3.0.1/package.jsonld
An SPDX 3.0.1 document in JSON-LD format.
.Nm
uses
.Xr spdxtool 1
to create it.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
replaces a document only after it creates the new document without error.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl c
Remove the documents that have no SBOM file.
This removes the documents of packages that you removed.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ".Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH"
.It Ev LOCALBASE
The base directory of installed packages.
The port build sets the default value.
.It Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
If set,
.Xr bomtool 1
and
.Xr spdxtool 1
use this UNIX timestamp as the creation time of the documents.
Two runs with the same SBOM files and the same value then create the
same documents.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
sets
.Ev PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR
to the
.Pa share/sbom/pc
directory and unsets
.Ev PKG_CONFIG_PATH
and
.Ev PKG_CONFIG_PRELOADED_FILES .
The tools then find SBOM files only.
They do not find the regular
.Xr pkgconf 1
modules.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa ${LOCALBASE}/share/sbom/spdx-3.0.1/"
.It Pa ${LOCALBASE}/share/sbom/pc/
The SBOM files that the packages install.
.It Pa ${LOCALBASE}/share/sbom/spdx-2.2/
The SPDX 2.2 documents.
.It Pa ${LOCALBASE}/share/sbom/spdx-3.0.1/
The SPDX 3.0.1 documents.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
.Nm
writes a message to standard error if it cannot create a document.
Then it continues with the next package.
This can occur when an SBOM file lists a dependency that has no SBOM file.
At the end,
.Nm
exits with a value of 1.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create the documents for all installed packages:
.Pp
.Dl # sbom-generator
.Pp
Create the documents for the
.Dq curl
package only:
.Pp
.Dl # sbom-generator curl
.Pp
Create all documents again and remove the documents of packages that you removed:
.Pp
.Dl # sbom-generator -c
.Pp
Create documents that are the same each time:
.Pp
.Dl # SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=0 sbom-generator
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bomtool 1 ,
.Xr pkgconf 1 ,
.Xr spdxtool 1 ,
.Xr pc 5
